[center][size=6][b]Val's DnD AIO Beyond Patch[/b][/size]
[size=3][i]Per-character toggles for the rules of DnD 5.5e All-in-One BEYOND[/i][/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What is this?[/b][/size]
A small add-on for [url=https://github.com/Yoonmoonsik/bg3dnd][b]DnD 5.5e All-in-One BEYOND[/b][/url] by Yoonmoonsik. It adds two toggle passives that switch off some of that mod's rules, character by character.

[b]Both toggles start OFF.[/b] Installing the patch changes nothing until you turn one on, so you keep everything the original mod does and opt out only of the rules you don't want.

[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
Every party member gets two toggles on the passive bar. Turn them on or off per character at any time, and the change takes effect immediately.

[size=4][b]Spell Freedom[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Removes the [b]One Spell with a Spell Slot per Turn[/b] rule, so you can cast more than one leveled spell per turn again (for example, one with your action and one with your bonus action).
[*]While it's on, the rule's passive is removed from the character sheet. Turn it off and the passive comes back.
[*][b]Swift Witchcraft rework:[/b] the feat only existed to get around that rule. With Spell Freedom on, it still gives +1 INT/WIS/CHA, and its action becomes a [b]free Quickened Spell once per Short Rest[/b]: the next spell you cast that turn that costs an action costs a bonus action instead.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Vanilla Short Rests[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Short rests heal like the base game again (half your max HP, or full HP with Durable or the "short rest heals to full" custom setting), instead of healing 1 HP and unlocking "Use Hit Point Dice".
[*]Hit Point Dice are still there for the features that spend them (Durable, Lifedrinker, Sangromancy, Dwarven Fortitude, etc.).
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/baldursgate3/mods/2172][b]BG3 Script Extender[/b][/url]
[*][url=https://github.com/Yoonmoonsik/bg3dnd][b]DnD 5.5e All-in-One BEYOND[/b][/url] (the original, unmodified)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install BG3 Script Extender and DnD 5.5e All-in-One BEYOND.
[*]Install this patch with your mod manager (BG3 Mod Manager or Vortex), or drop the .pak into your Mods folder.
[*]Load the patch [b]after[/b] DnD 5.5e All-in-One BEYOND. BG3 Mod Manager sorts this automatically.
[*]In game, turn on the toggles you want on each character's passive bar.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Save Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Adding the patch to an existing campaign:[/b] safe. With both toggles off, nothing changes.
[*][b]Removing the patch:[/b] safe. The original rules come back on the next load.
[*]As always, back up your save before changing your mod list.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Not compatible with Val's Variant: DnD 5.5e All-In-One Beyond[/b] (the full fork). Use the original mod plus this patch instead.
[*]Other mods that change the same rules (the one-spell-per-turn rule, short rest healing, or Swift Witchcraft) may conflict. Whichever mod loads last wins.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Known Issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The Swift Witchcraft [b]feat description[/b] (in the feat picker and on its passive) still shows the original text. The new action and its effect have the correct text.
[*]With Vanilla Short Rests on, the "Use Hit Point Dice" action stays in Common Actions, greyed out.
[*]The patch's new text is [b]English only[/b].
[/list]

Found a bug? Please report it in the Bugs tab with your load order and what happened.

[line]

